<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Shifts' cross-section surface, carved into its own leaf project because most of its
    consumers are still in Base: DashboardService and AdminDashboardService build the
    home and admin dashboards off IShiftView and IShiftManagementServiceRead,
    AccountDeletionService cancels signups and drops volunteer profiles,
    UserParticipationBackfillService reads the active burn (SuspendNonCompliantMembersJob
    used to read it here too; its body became NonCompliantMemberSuspension inside
    Humans.Users at G5 lane 4b-2d and the job itself followed at lane 5b-4,
    nobodies-collective/Humans#866), and ShiftVolunteerSearchBuilder / the Shell
    authorization handlers read the
    coordinator surface. A Contracts/ *folder* inside Humans.Shifts would therefore make
    Base reference a section and cycle (design §15.5b,
    memory/architecture/section-project-cycle-fix.md).

    The split is carved from the call sites, not from the interfaces (Notifications'
    rule). A member is on this leaf if something outside the section calls it, and
    nowhere else. From IShiftManagementService that is the cross-section reads
    (IShiftManagementServiceRead), the volunteer-profile surface Shell's profile page
    and widget gallery read (IShiftVolunteerProfiles), and the dev-fixture verbs
    Humans.Development's seeder needs (IShiftSeeding); the rota/shift generation,
    coordinator-dashboard and post-event-stats surface has no outside caller and stays
    on the internal IShiftManagementService, which inherits the three leaf interfaces so
    the section's own call sites are unchanged. Same shape for IShiftSignupService: the
    signup state machine Shell and onboarding drive leaves as IShiftSignups, the seeder's
    verbs as IShiftSignupSeeding (Teams' rule — the seeder builds a multi-section
    fixture, so the verbs come to the leaf rather than the seeding going into the
    section), and the review surface stays internal.

    References Humans.Interfaces (IApplicationService, IInvalidator, SurfaceBudget,
    Grandfathered) and nothing else. The Humans.Domain reference is gone as of G5 lane
    4b-2k: it existed for the section's persisted-string enums (SignupStatus, ShiftPeriod,
    ShiftPriority, RotaPeriod, BuildSubPeriod, SignupPolicy), and those now live here, in
    Humans.Shifts.Contracts, because this leaf's own signatures name them (Budget's rule).
    Their EnumStringStabilityTests rows live in tests/Humans.Shifts.Tests/Enums.

    No entity crosses this boundary. Shift / ShiftSignup / Rota / EventSettings /
    VolunteerEventProfile are internal sealed types in Humans.Shifts.Domain, and every
    leaf member that used to return one returns a flat projection instead
    (ShiftUserSummary, UrgentShiftInfo / ShiftInfo / RotaInfo, ShiftVolunteerProfileInfo,
    BurnSettingsInfo, and Guid ids on the seeding verbs).
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Humans.Base\Humans.Base.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="NodaTime" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
